I disagree with the value of power gloves to combat wombats.
Once strength is maxed they only help for a valk who wishes
to throw Mojo.  The damage when Mojo's return flight is not
caught is enough that I rarely wish to throw it.  My version
goes:

for combat wombat leather < power < dexterity

With power and dexterity preference very ambiguous earlier
in the game then growing more pronounced as the game
progresses.

for spell caster power < leather < dexterity

With power and leather preference very ambiguous earlier
in the game but as soon as dexterity comes available the
difference is large enough that power or leather get dropped.

Increased dexterity adds to the to-hit role but maxed out luck
and skill and enchantment see to it that swings/shots never
miss so that feature is redundant.  But it also helps for doors
and traps and such if I understand dexterity correctly.  It's
a subtle but useful advantage.

The choice among head gear is more complex.  A spell caster
may want an elven leather helmet until corun-mumble or
brilliance is found but a character without infravision benefits
from ESP enough that it remains useful throughout.  A
combat wombat might want to use a drawvish iron helmet
early on but a similar late tradeoff between brilliance and ESP
happens.  With helmets, visored have an advantage that can
push the difference one way or another.


